| **TARS** | ? | Conclusion mismatch + fabricated real-world claims |
| DualRes | 2.5 | Valid method, overstates theory, missing ablations |
| Dens3R | 6.0 | Missing depth evaluation but strong on other fronts |

TARS's core simulation work (novel visuo-tactile point cloud, clean ablation design) is legitimate and nontrivial—this keeps it above the zero-result papers. But the combination of (a) a conclusion describing a different paper and (b) an outright unsupported real-world deployment claim places it firmly in the clear reject range. These weaknesses are structural and severe enough to qualify as fundamental issues that undermine the paper's core claims.

Relative to calibration: more severe issues than DualRes (2.5), comparable severity to Exploitable Negotiators (0.5) and TabPalooza (1.2). The legitimate ablation experiments prevent it from joining the 0.5 tier, but the dual major weaknesses keep it below anything above 2.0.

