The paper's promising results for Linear Probability Models and broad experimental scope are positive aspects, but they cannot compensate for the fatal flaw of missing the proper baseline comparison. Without this, the paper's central claim about advancing the size-accuracy Pareto frontier remains unsubstantiated.

Given the severity of the methodological flaws and their direct impact on the core claims, I assign a score in line with similar papers in the calibration set that have fundamental methodological issues.

